      "help_url": "https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port#readme",
      "warnings": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Supply your matching original",
          "instruction": "For the managed Windows route, choose your own exact GoldenEye 007 NTSC-U USA big-endian .z64 original. Portcove verifies its declared identity and copies it to data/ge007.ntsc-final.z64 beside the player. PAL, Japanese, byte-swapped and modified images are not accepted by this contract. No BIOS or separate installer is required."
        },
        {
          "title": "Choose Play for first-run preparation",
          "instruction": "Keep the complete official Windows ZIP together. Play starts ge007.x86_64.exe, which invokes its bundled frozen converter when generated sidecars are missing. Portcove does not run a discovered helper during download or setup, and does not certify successful upstream conversion or gameplay. If conversion fails, follow the selected upstream troubleshooting instructions and keep your original and saves recoverable."
        },
        {
          "title": "Keep an existing copy recoverable",
          "instruction": "For an external copy, select ge007.x86_64.exe with its containing folder as working directory, save launch details, then choose Play. Preserve its data/ge007.ntsc-final.z64, data/ge007.eep, data/ge007.ini, emulator-import backup files and ppm screenshots, plus any custom locations you selected. You or upstream provide external updates; Portcove registration does not update, back up or delete those files. Generated sidecars and shader lists belong to their runtime version. Optional Python/source tools remain separate deliberate upstream actions; extra bytecode or arbitrary tool output can require preservation before managed replacement."
        }
      ]
    }
  },
